<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.12.7: Lesson Synthesis</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01070</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.12.7: Lesson Synthesis</md:title>
    <md:uuid>f13e1dbe-252f-41b5-a666-4fbabb267555</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Tell students that function \(q\) gives the number of minutes a person sleeps as a function of the number of hours
  they sleep in a 24-hour period. Display a graphic organizer such as shown.</para>
  <table class="os-raise-midsizetable">
    <thead>
      <row>
        <entry><emphasis> </emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>in the domain?</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>in the range?</emphasis></entry></row>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <row>  
      <entry>
        negative values
      </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        0
      </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        values less than 1
      </entry>
      <entry/>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        24
      </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        25
      </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
       60
      </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        fractions
      </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
      values greater than 480
      </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        1,500
      </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>

<para>Ask students to decide whether each value or set of values described in the first column could be in the domain and
  in the range of the function. They should be prepared to explain their decisions (some of which may depend on the
  assumptions they made about the situation).</para>
<para>Once the class completes the organizer (an example is shown here), give students a moment to come up with a holistic
  description of the domain and range of this function.</para>
  <table class="os-raise-midsizetable">
    <thead>
      <row>
        <entry><emphasis> </emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>in the domain?</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>in the range?</emphasis></entry></row>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <row>  
      <entry>
        negative values
      </entry>
      <entry>no</entry>
      <entry>no</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        0
      </entry>
      <entry>yes</entry>
      <entry>yes</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        values less than 1
      </entry>
      <entry>yes</entry>
      <entry>yes</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        24
      </entry>
      <entry>yes</entry>
      <entry>yes</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        25
      </entry>
      <entry>no</entry>
      <entry>yes</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
       60
      </entry>
      <entry>no</entry>
      <entry>yes</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        fractions
      </entry>
      <entry>yes</entry>
      <entry>yes</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
      values greater than 480
      </entry>
      <entry>no</entry>
      <entry>yes</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        1,500
      </entry>
      <entry>no</entry>
      <entry>no</entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>
</section>
</content>
